691 \\times 1531 = 691 \\times 1000 + 691 \\times 531$.\n\n$691 \\times 1000 = 691000$.\n$691 \\times 500 = 345500$.\n$691 \\times 31 = 21421$.\n$691 \\times 531 = 345500 + 21421 = 366921$.\nTotal: $691000 + 366921 = 1057921$.\n\n$1057921 / 3125 = 338.53472...$\n\n$3125 \\times 338 = 1056250$.\n\n$1057921 - 1056250 = 1671$.\n\nSo $691 \\times 1531 \\equiv 1671 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nNext: $1671 \\times 466 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$1671 \\times 466 = 1671 \\times 400 + 1671 \\times 66$.\n\n$1671 \\times 400 = 668400$.\n$1671 \\times 66 = 1671 \\times 60 + 1671 \\times 6 = 100260 + 10026 = 110286$.\nTotal: $668400 + 110286 = 778686$.\n\n$778686 / 3125 = 249.17952...$\n\n$3125 \\times 249 = 778125$.\n\n$778686 - 778125 = 561$.\n\nSo $1671 \\times 466 \\equiv 561 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nNext: $561 \\times 1971 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$561 \\times 1971 = 561 \\times 2000 - 561 \\times 29$.\n\n$561 \\times 2000 = 1122000$.\n$561 \\times 29 = 561 \\times 30 - 561 = 16830 - 561 = 16269$.\n$1122000 - 16269 = 1105731$.\n\n$1105731 / 3125 = 353.83392...$\n\n$3125 \\times 353 = 1103125$.\n\n$1105731 - 1103125 = 2606$.\n\nSo $561 \\times 1971 \\equiv 2606 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nNext: $2606 \\times 2003 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$2606 \\times 2003 = 2606 \\times 2000 + 2606 \\times 3$.\n\n$2606 \\times 2000 = 5212000$.\n$2606 \\times 3 = 7818$.\nTotal: $5212000 + 7818 = 5219818$.\n\n$5219818 / 3125 = 1670.34176...$\n\n$3125 \\times 1670 = 5218750$.\n\n$5219818 - 5218750 = 1068$.\n\nSo $2003^{625} \\equiv 1068 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nLet me double-check this computation. Let me re-verify some of the squaring steps.\n\nActually, let me re-verify $a_1 = 2003^2 \\mod 3125$.\n\n$2003^2 = 4012009$. $4012009 / 3125 = 1283.842...$. $1283 \\times 3125 = 1283 \\times 3000 + 1283 \\times 125 = 3849000 + 160375 = 4009375$. $4012009 - 4009375 = 2634$. ✓\n\n$a_2 = 2634^2 \\mod 3125$. $2634^2$: $2600^2 = 6760000$, $2 \\times 2600 \\times 34 = 176800$, $34^2 = 1156$. Total: $6760000 + 176800 + 1156 = 6937956$. ✓\n\n$6937956 / 3125 = 2220.14...$. $2220 \\times 3125 = 2220 \\times 3000 + 2220 \\times 125 = 6660000 + 277500 = 6937500$. $6937956 - 6937500 = 456$. ✓\n\n$a_3 = 456^2 = 207936$. $207936 / 3125 = 66.53...$. $66 \\times 3125 = 206250$. $207936 - 206250 = 1686$. ✓\n\n$a_4 = 1686^2 \\mod 3125$. $1686^2$: $1686 \\times 1686$. $1686 \\times 1000 = 1686000$, $1686 \\times 686 = 1686 \\times 700 - 1686 \\times 14 = 1180200 - 23604 = 1156596$. Total: $1686000 + 1156596 = 2842596$. ✓\n\n$2842596 / 3125 = 909.63...$. $909 \\times 3125 = 909 \\times 3000 + 909 \\times 125 = 2727000 + 113625 = 2840625$. $2842596 - 2840625 = 1971$. ✓\n\n$a_5 = 1971^2 \\mod 3125$. $1971^2 = (2000-29)^2 = 4000000 - 116000 + 841 = 3884841$. ✓\n\n$3884841 / 3125 = 1243.14...$. $1243 \\times 3125 = 1243 \\times 3000 + 1243 \\times 125 = 3729000 + 155375 = 3884375$. $3884841 - 3884375 = 466$. ✓\n\n$a_6 = 466^2 = 217156$. $217156 / 3125 = 69.49...$. $69 \\times 3125 = 215625$. $217156 - 215625 = 1531$. ✓\n\n$a_7 = 1531^2 \\mod 3125$. $1531^2 = (1500+31)^2 = 2250000 + 93000 + 961 = 2343961$. ✓\n\n$2343961 / 3125 = 750.07...$. $750 \\times 3125 = 2343750$. $2343961 - 2343750 = 211$. ✓\n\n$a_8 = 211^2 = 44521$. $44521 / 3125 = 14.25...$. $14 \\times 3125 = 43750$. $44521 - 43750 = 771$. ✓\n\n$a_9 = 771^2 = 594441$. $594441 / 3125 = 190.22...$. $190 \\times 3125 = 593750$. $594441 - 593750 = 691$. ✓\n\nNow the multiplication chain:\n\n$691 \\times 1531$: $691 \\times 1531$. Let me verify. $691 \\times 1500 = 1036500$. $691 \\times 31 = 21421$. Total: $1036500 + 21421 = 1057921$. ✓\n\n$1057921 / 3125 = 338.53...$. $338 \\times 3125 = 338 \\times 3000 + 338 \\times 125 = 1014000 + 42250 = 1056250$. $1057921 - 1056250 = 1671$. ✓\n\n$1671 \\times 466$: $1671 \\times 466$. $1671 \\times 400 = 668400$. $1671 \\times 66 = 110286$. Total: $778686$. ✓\n\n$778686 / 3125 = 249.18...$. $249 \\times 3125 = 249 \\times 3000 + 249 \\times 125 = 747000 + 31125 = 778125$. $778686 - 778125 = 561$. ✓\n\n$561 \\times 1971$: $561 \\times 2000 = 1122000$. $561 \\times 29 = 16269$. $1122000 - 16269 = 1105731$. ✓\n\n$1105731 / 3125 = 353.83...$. $353 \\times 3125 = 353 \\times 3000 + 353 \\times 125 = 1059000 + 44125 = 1103125$. $1105731 - 1103125 = 2606$. ✓\n\n$2606 \\times 2003$: $2606 \\times 2000 = 5212000$. $2606 \\times 3 = 7818$. Total: $5219818$. ✓\n\n$5219818 / 3125 = 1670.34...$. $1670 \\times 3125 = 1670 \\times 3000 + 1670 \\times 125 = 5010000 + 208750 = 5218750$. $5219818 - 5218750 = 1068$. ✓\n\nSo $2003^{625} \\equiv 1068 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n**CRT: Now combine:**\n- $N \\equiv 3 \\pmod{32}$\n- $N \\equiv 1068 \\pmod{3125}$\n\nI need $x$ such that $x \\equiv 3 \\pmod{32}$ and $x \\equiv 1068 \\pmod{3125}$, with $0 \\le x < 100000$.\n\n$x = 3125k + 1068$ for some integer $k$, $0 \\le k \\le 31$.\n\n$3125k + 1068 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{32}$.\n\n$3125 \\mod 32$: $32 \\times 97 = 3104$. $3125 - 3104 = 21$. So $3125 \\equiv 21 \\pmod{32}$.\n\n$1068 \\mod 32$: $32 \\times 33 = 1056$. $1068 - 1056 = 12$. So $1068 \\equiv 12 \\pmod{32}$.\n\n$21k + 12 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{32}$.\n\n$21k \\equiv -9 \\equiv 23 \\pmod{32}$.\n\nI need the inverse of $21 \\mod 32$. $21 \\times 3 = 63 = 64 - 1 \\equiv -1 \\pmod{32}$. So $21 \\times (-3) \\equiv 1 \\pmod{32}$, i.e., $21 \\times 29 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{32}$ (since $-3 \\equiv 29$).\n\nCheck: $21 \\times 29 = 609$. $609 / 32 = 19.03...$. $19 \\times 32 = 608$. $609 - 608 = 1$. ✓\n\nSo $k \\equiv 23 \\times 29 \\pmod{32}$.\n\n$23 \\times 29 = 667$. $667 / 32 = 20.84...$. $20 \\times 32 = 640$. $667 - 640 = 27$.\n\nSo $k \\equiv 27 \\pmod{32}$.\n\n$k = 27$.\n\n$x = 3125 \\times 27 + 1068 = 84375 + 1068 = 85443$.\n\nLet me verify: $85443 \\mod 32$: $32 \\times 2670 = 85440$. $85443 - 85440 = 3$. ✓\n\n$85443 \\mod 3125$: $3125 \\times 27 = 84375$. $85443 - 84375 = 1068$. ✓\n\nSo the last 5 digits are $\\boxed{85443}$.\n\nWait, let me double-check the whole chain once more, especially the exponent reduction.\n\nWe need $2003^{2005^{2007}} \\mod 100000$.\n\n$100000 = 32 \\times 3125$, $\\gcd(32, 3125) = 1$. CRT applies.\n\n**Mod 32:**\n$2003 \\equiv 19 \\pmod{32}$.\n$\\phi(32) = 16$, $\\gcd(19, 32) = 1$.\n$2005^{2007} \\mod 16$: $2005 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{16}$, need $5^{2007} \\mod 16$.\n$\\phi(16) = 8$, $2007 \\equiv 7 \\pmod{8}$.\n$5^7 \\mod 16$: $5^2 = 25 \\equiv 9$, $5^4 \\equiv 81 \\equiv 1$, $5^7 = 5^4 \\cdot 5^2 \\cdot 5 \\equiv 1 \\cdot 9 \\cdot 5 = 45 \\equiv 13$.\nSo $2005^{2007} \\equiv 13 \\pmod{16}$.\n$19^{13} \\mod 32$: $19^2 \\equiv 361 \\equiv 9$, $19^4 \\equiv 81 \\equiv 17$, $19^8 \\equiv 289 \\equiv 1$, $19^{13} = 19^8 \\cdot 19^4 \\cdot 19 \\equiv 1 \\cdot 17 \\cdot 19 = 323 \\equiv 3$.\nSo $N \\equiv 3 \\pmod{32}$. ✓\n\n**Mod 3125:**\n$2003 \\equiv 2003 \\pmod{3125}$, $\\gcd(2003, 3125) = 1$.\n$\\phi(3125) = 2500$.\n$2005^{2007} \\mod 2500$.\n$2500 = 4 \\times 625$.\nMod 4: $2005 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$, so $2005^{2007} \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$.\nMod 625: $2005 \\equiv 130 \\pmod{625}$, $130 = 5 \\times 26$, $130^{2007} = 5^{2007} \\times 26^{2007}$. Since $5^4 = 625$, $5^{2007} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{625}$. So $130^{2007} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{625}$.\nCRT: $x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$, $x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{625}$. $x = 625k$, $625 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$, so $k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$, $k=1$, $x = 625$.\nSo $2005^{2007} \\equiv 625 \\pmod{2500}$.\n$2003^{625} \\mod 3125 = 1068$ (computed above). ✓\n\n**CRT:**\n$x \\equiv 3 \\pmod{32}$, $x \\equiv 1068 \\pmod{3125}$.\n$x = 3125k + 1068$, $21k + 12 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{32}$, $21k \\equiv 23 \\pmod{32}$, $k \\equiv 23 \\times 29 \\equiv 27 \\pmod{32}$.\n$x = 3125 \\times 27 + 1068 = 85443$.\n\nThe last 5 digits are **85443**.\n\nHmm, let me just double-check the $2005^{2007} \\mod 2500$ computation once more, since that's the trickiest part.\n\n$2005^{2007} \\mod 2500$ where $2500 = 2^2 \\cdot 5^4 = 4 \\cdot 625$.\n\nMod 4: $2005 \\equiv 1 \\pmod 4$, so $1^{2007} = 1$. ✓\n\nMod 625: $2005 \\equiv 130 \\pmod{625}$. $130 = 2 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 13$. $130^{2007} = 2^{2007} \\cdot 5^{2007} \\cdot 13^{2007}$. Since $5^{2007}$ has $5^{2007}$ and $625 = 5^4$, and $2007 \\ge 4$, we have $5^{2007} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{625}$. So $130^{2007} \\equiv 0 \\pmod{625}$. ✓\n\nCRT: $x \\equiv 0 \\pmod{625}$, $x \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$. $x = 625k$, $625k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$, $625 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$, so $k \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$. Smallest positive: $k=1$, $x=625$. Check: $625 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{625}$ ✓, $625 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{4}$ ✓. ✓\n\nSo $2005^{2007} \\equiv 625 \\pmod{2500}$. ✓\n\nAnd then $2003^{2005^{2007}} \\equiv 2003^{625} \\pmod{3125}$ by Euler's theorem (since $\\gcd(2003, 3125) = 1$ and $\\phi(3125) = 2500$, and $2005^{2007} \\equiv 625 \\pmod{2500}$). ✓\n\nEverything checks out. The answer is 85443.\n\nActually, let me also sanity-check by verifying $2003^{625} \\mod 3125$ using a slightly different method. Let me verify using the fact that $2003 \\equiv -1122 \\pmod{3125}$... that's not simpler.\n\nLet me instead verify a few of the intermediate products differently.\n\n$2003^{625} = 2003^{512} \\cdot 2003^{64} \\cdot 2003^{32} \\cdot 2003^{16} \\cdot 2003^1$.\n\nWe computed:\n- $2003^1 \\equiv 2003$\n- $2003^{16} \\equiv 1971$\n- $2003^{32} \\equiv 466$\n- $2003^{64} \\equiv 1531$\n- $2003^{512} \\equiv 691$\n\nProduct: $691 \\times 1531 \\times 466 \\times 1971 \\times 2003$.\n\nLet me try a different grouping. $(691 \\times 466) \\times (1531 \\times 1971) \\times 2003$.\n\n$691 \\times 466$: $691 \\times 466 = 691 \\times 400 + 691 \\times 66 = 276400 + 45606 = 322006$.\n\n$322006 / 3125 = 103.04...$. $103 \\times 3125 = 321875$. $322006 - 321875 = 131$.\n\nSo $691 \\times 466 \\equiv 131 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$1531 \\times 1971$: $1531 \\times 1971 = 1531 \\times 2000 - 1531 \\times 29 = 3062000 - 44399 = 3017601$.\n\n$3017601 / 3125 = 965.63...$. $965 \\times 3125 = 3015625$. $3017601 - 3015625 = 1976$.\n\nSo $1531 \\times 1971 \\equiv 1976 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nNow: $131 \\times 1976 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\n$131 \\times 1976 = 131 \\times 2000 - 131 \\times 24 = 262000 - 3144 = 258856$.\n\n$258856 / 3125 = 82.83...$. $82 \\times 3125 = 256250$. $258856 - 256250 = 2606$.\n\nSo $131 \\times 1976 \\equiv 2606 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nNow: $2606 \\times 2003 \\pmod{3125}$.\n\nThis is the same as before: $2606 \\times 2003 = 5219818$. $5219818 - 5218750 = 1068$. ✓\n\nGreat, both groupings give $1068$. The answer is confirmed.\n\nThe last 5 digits of $N = 2003^{2005^{2007}}$ are $\\boxed{85443}$.", "tool_calls": [], "created_at": 1786680988}
